Subject: [PATCH] em: the state machines' per-tick lines and the remaining per-message dumps to the debug channel

After 0237, through a room catalog on rdk-1004 (6 October 2026), em_ctrl's journal still
passed its cap in bursts (journald dropping 1,233 and 2,994 lines in two 30 s windows of
the first nine minutes). What filled it: the state machines' "unhandled state" and
"unhandled case" lines, printed for every radio at every tick it spends in a state with no
handler (about a quarter); the policy lookup's trace of every comparison; each candidate
query's completion (the query's own result line stays); the native backhaul module's
per-sample observation; and the AP capability and M2 dumps, repeated at each renewal, one of
them printing every network's passphrase.

Those 62 statements now print through em_util_dbg_print as in 0237 (EM_CONF for the code
the agent shares, EM_CTRL for the controller's own); the M2 line names the SSID and its
authentication without the passphrase, also when debugging. What stays on the journal:
errors and validation failures, Topology Responses and Notifications received, each
candidate query's result, renewals, the WSC exchange's messages.

Upstream-Status: Pending

